IncreaseLiquidityIntegrationConcreteTest
├── When the caller is not the owner
│   └── It should revert with {OwnableUnauthorizedAccount}
└── When the caller is the owner
    ├── When the locker is not locked
    │   └── It should revert with {NotLocked}
    └── When the locker is locked 
        ├── When both amounts are zero
        │   └── It should revert with {ZeroAmount}
        └── When one of the amounts is not zero 
            ├── When the amounts deposited are smaller than the minimum amounts
            │   └── It should revert with {PSC}
            └── When the amounts deposited are greater than or equal to the minimum amounts
                ├── When the locker balance is smaller than the amounts
                │   ├── When the locker is not staked
                │   │   ├── When the locker balance is smaller than the supplied amount
                │   │   │   ├── It should mint new liquidity for the locker
                │   │   │   ├── It should increase the lp amount
                │   │   │   ├── It should refund all leftover tokens to the locker owner
                │   │   │   ├── It should clear outstanding allowances
                │   │   │   └── It should emit a {LiquidityIncreased} event
                │   │   └── When the locker balance is greater than or equal to the supplied amount
                │   │       ├── It should mint new liquidity for the locker
                │   │       ├── It should increase the lp amount
                │   │       ├── It should refund the supplied amount to the locker owner
                │   │       ├── It should clear outstanding allowances
                │   │       └── It should emit a {LiquidityIncreased} event
                │   └── When the locker is staked
                │       ├── When the locker balance is smaller than the supplied amount_
                │       │   ├── It should mint new liquidity for the locker
                │       │   ├── It should increase the lp amount
                │       │   ├── It should refund all leftover tokens to the locker owner
                │       │   ├── It should deposit the additional liquidity in the gauge
                │       │   ├── It should clear outstanding allowances
                │       │   └── It should emit a {LiquidityIncreased} event
                │       └── When the locker balance is greater than or equal to the supplied amount_
                │           ├── It should mint new liquidity for the locker
                │           ├── It should increase the lp amount
                │           ├── It should refund the supplied amount to the locker owner
                │           ├── It should deposit the additional liquidity in the gauge
                │           ├── It should clear outstanding allowances
                │           └── It should emit a {LiquidityIncreased} event
                └── When the locker balance is not smaller than the amounts
                    ├── When the locker is not staked_
                    │   ├── It should mint new liquidity for the locker
                    │   ├── It should increase the lp amount
                    │   ├── It should refund leftover tokens back to the locker
                    │   ├── It should clear outstanding allowances
                    │   └── It should emit a {LiquidityIncreased} event
                    └── When the locker is staked_
                        ├── It should mint new liquidity for the locker
                        ├── It should increase the lp amount
                        ├── It should refund leftover tokens back to the locker
                        ├── It should deposit the additional liquidity in the gauge
                        ├── It should clear outstanding allowances
                        └── It should emit a {LiquidityIncreased} event
